What does this print?
int i, s = 0;
for (i = 1; i <= 10; i++) { if (i % 3 == 0) continue; s += i; }
printf("%d", s);

What is printed?
void f(int x) { x = 10; }
int main() { int a = 5; f(a); printf("%d", a); }

What is printed?
void f(int *x) { *x = 10; }
int main() { int a = 5; f(&a); printf("%d", a); }

Consider:
int x = 1;
void f() { printf("%d", x); }
void g() { int x = 2; f(); }
main calls g(). What is printed under static scoping and under dynamic scoping?

